abstract: >-
  This focused conceptual paper defines unification in UOHF as using one coherent
  semantic system to describe human functions as they exist within an integrated
  whole person, together with their functional engagement under internal and
  external demands. It clarifies the relations among human function, demand,
  bodily structure, bodily process, coordination, compensation, boundaries,
  state, time, and change.
